Utility Determine Next Occurrence V2 (2017-03-03)
* Initial version.  See README for details.

Utility Determine Next Occurrence V2 (2026-10-20)
* Upgraded the IceCube library from 0.14.0 to 0.16.4.  0.14.0 used the Fixnum
  class, which was removed in Ruby 3.2, so weekly, monthly absolute and yearly
  schedules failed on JRuby 10 with "uninitialized constant ... Fixnum".
  0.16.4 still runs on older JRuby versions (Ruby 2.x).
* Weekly schedules now use the Weekdays even when a Timing value is present.
  Previously any Timing value caused the Weekdays to be ignored and the
  schedule to fire every day.
* Fixed validation that never ran (operator precedence), so a missing Interval,
  Timing or weekday index is now reported instead of silently producing a
  schedule that fires every day.
* Unrecognized Months, Weekdays, weekday index or Days of Month values, and an
  Interval that isn't a whole number of 1 or more, now raise a clear error.
  Blank entries in comma separated lists (ex: a trailing comma) are ignored.
* A schedule that can never occur (ex: February 30) now raises an error
  instead of hanging the Task engine thread.
* A Start value with no offset is read as UTC, as documented, rather than as
  the server's local time.
* The next_occurrence result is always returned in UTC
  (ex: 2018-03-02 22:00:00 UTC), as documented.  Previously it used the
  offset of the Start value (ex: +0000).
